digraph GSN {
  rankdir=TB;
  node [fontname="Helvetica" fontsize=9];
  edge [fontname="Helvetica" fontsize=8];
  labelloc="t"; label="SafeDSE safety argument — v_nvp"; fontname="Helvetica";
  C1 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C1\nIEC 61508 is the governing functional\nsafety standard; integrity is allocated as\na Safety Integrity Level per actor (Q1,\nQ13)."];
  C2 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C2\nPlatform: 34 core slots across 13 fault\ncontainment regions, core types cortexM,\ncortexR, ppcE200, sparcLEON. Cores\nactually instantiated in this solution:\n[1, 2, 7, 13, 14, 29]."];
  C3 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C3\nApplications: c_rasta, modelled as\nsynchronous dataflow graphs and unfolded\nto an equivalent homogeneous graph before\nmapping."];
  C4 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C4\nFault model under consideration:\nUNDETERMINED (Q2). Patterns not covering\nthis fault class were excluded from the\ndesign space, and placement relations\nmotivated only by an excluded fault class\nwere not posted."];
  J1 [shape=ellipse style=filled fillcolor="#fff6d5" label="J1 (J)\nThis argument is generated from a design\nspace exploration result. It argues only\nover properties of the ARCHITECTURE and\nits DEPLOYMENT: which pattern is applied\nto which actor, where components are\nplaced relative to each other, how\nintegrity levels are provisioned per core,\nand whether the resulting schedule meets\nits timing requirement. Claims about\nimplementation correctness, detection\ncoverage and development process are\noutside what a mapping can establish and\nare carried below as undeveloped goals."];
  A1 [shape=ellipse style=filled fillcolor="#fff6d5" label="A1 (A)\nThe worst-case execution times supplied to\nthe exploration are sound upper bounds for\nevery actor on every core type it may be\nbound to. The exploration consumes these\nfigures; it does not establish them."];
  A2 [shape=ellipse style=filled fillcolor="#fff6d5" label="A2 (A)\nToken preservation (Q4): every replica\nfires on every iteration and produces on\nall of its outputs, in the fault-free and\nin the degraded case alike. Detection\nmarks a token invalid; it never withholds\none. The timing argument therefore holds\nin the degraded mode, at the cost of being\nconservative when no fault is present."];
  G1 [shape=box label="G1\nThe deployed architecture of v_nvp\npreserves the allocated safety integrity\nof every safety-related actor."];
  S1 [shape=parallelogram label="S1\nArgument over each safety-related actor in\nturn, followed by the platform-wide\nproperties on which those per-actor\narguments depend."];
  G2 [shape=box label="G2\nActor frontEnd of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 3, attains SIL 3 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C5 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C5\nfrontEnd is unfolded into 1 concurrent\ncopy, bound to core 1, implemented at SIL\n3."];
  Sn1 [shape=circle label="Sn1\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of frontEnd is\nimplemented at or above its allocated SIL\nand runs on a core provisioned to at least\nthat level."];
  G3 [shape=box label="G3\nEvery copy of frontEnd is implemented at\nSIL 3 or above and is not hosted on a core\nprovisioned below that level."];
  C6 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C6\nComponents introduced by nvp_three_version\nfor frontEnd: version_2 on core 7 at SIL\n3; version_3 on core 29 at SIL 3; voter on\ncore 7 at SIL 3."];
  S2 [shape=parallelogram label="S2\nArgument by application of the\nnvp_three_version safety architecture\npattern, over each of its general\nscenarios."];
  C7 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C7\nPattern nvp_three_version [Armoush 2010,\nIEC 61508-7 C.4.4]: N-version programming\nwith three independently developed\nversions and an explicit majority voter.\nThe versions compute from the same inputs\nand the voter selects the majority result,\nmasking a fault in any one version.\nAttainable SIL [3, 4]; covers random_hw,\nsystematic_sw; fails masking; voter\nexplicit."];
  G4 [shape=box label="G4\nA fault in any single version is masked by\nthe majority of the remaining versions.\n[nvp_three_version/SC1]"];
  S3 [shape=parallelogram label="S3\nAchieved through the Voting tactic\n(Masking): Mask the failure of a subsystem\nso that the failure does not propagate to\nother systems."];
  C8 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C8\nVoting: Voting makes a failure\ntransparent. It does not repair the\nfailure, but hides it by choosing a\ncorrect result from redundant subsystems,\ndeciding for the majority of the output\nvalues."];
  C9 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C9\nCandidate methods from the standard: IEC\n61508-7 A.1.4 voter; IEC 61508-7 A.6.5\ninput comparison/voting"];
  G5 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G5\nAn IEC 61508 method realising Voting is\nimplemented in frontEnd, and its\neffectiveness for the faults of concern is\ndemonstrated.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G6 [shape=box label="G6\nA random hardware fault affects at most\none of the three versions.\n[nvp_three_version/SC2]"];
  S4 [shape=parallelogram label="S4\nAchieved through the Replication\nRedundancy tactic (Redundancy):\nIntroduction of a redundant system which\nallows detection or masking of random\nhardware failures (not systematic\nfailures)."];
  C10 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C10\nReplication Redundancy: Introduction of a\nredundant system of the same\nimplementation. The redundant systems\nmaintain the same functionality, use\nidentical hardware, and run the same\nsoftware implementation."];
  G7 [shape=box label="G7\nIn the deployed mapping, the replicated\ncomponents are deployed on hardware that\ndoes not share a single point of random\nhardware failure."];
  Sn2 [shape=circle label="Sn2\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nDIFFERENT_FCR between frontEnd and\nfrontEnd/version_2: cores 1/7, fault\ncontainment regions 1/4, core types\ncortexR/ppcE200."];
  Sn3 [shape=circle label="Sn3\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nDIFFERENT_FCR between frontEnd and\nfrontEnd/version_3: cores 1/29, fault\ncontainment regions 1/11, core types\ncortexR/sparcLEON."];
  Sn4 [shape=circle label="Sn4\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nDIFFERENT_FCR between frontEnd/version_2\nand frontEnd/version_3: cores 7/29, fault\ncontainment regions 4/11, core types\nppcE200/sparcLEON."];
  Sn5 [shape=circle label="Sn5\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nDIFFERENT_FCR between frontEnd and\nfrontEnd/voter: cores 1/7, fault\ncontainment regions 1/4, core types\ncortexR/ppcE200."];
  C11 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C11\nCandidate methods from the standard: IEC\n61508-7 A.2.1 tests by redundant hardware;\nIEC 61508-7 A.2.5 monitored redundancy;\nIEC 61508-7 A.3.5 reciprocal comparison by\nsoftware; IEC 61508-7 A.4.5 block\nreplication; IEC 61508-7 A.6.3\nmulti-channel output; IEC 61508-7 A.7.3\ncomplete hardware redundancy; IEC 61508-7\nA.7.5 transmission redundancy"];
  G8 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G8\nAn IEC 61508 method realising Replication\nRedundancy is implemented in frontEnd, and\nits effectiveness for the faults of\nconcern is demonstrated.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G9 [shape=box label="G9\nA systematic fault in one version is not\nreproduced by the other two versions.\n[nvp_three_version/SC3]"];
  S5 [shape=parallelogram label="S5\nAchieved through the Diverse Redundancy\ntactic (Redundancy): Introduction of a\nredundant system which allows detection or\nmasking of failures in the specification\nor implementation as well as random\nhardware failures."];
  C12 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C12\nDiverse Redundancy: Redundant components\nuse different implementations which were\ndeveloped independently from the same\nspecification. Applied at specification\nlevel it further requires the requirement\nspecifications themselves to be produced\nby individual teams."];
  G10 [shape=box label="G10\nIn the deployed mapping, the diverse\ncomponents are deployed on distinct\nprocessor types."];
  Sn6 [shape=circle label="Sn6\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nDIVERSE between frontEnd and\nfrontEnd/version_2: cores 1/7, fault\ncontainment regions 1/4, core types\ncortexR/ppcE200."];
  Sn7 [shape=circle label="Sn7\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nDIVERSE between frontEnd and\nfrontEnd/version_3: cores 1/29, fault\ncontainment regions 1/11, core types\ncortexR/sparcLEON."];
  Sn8 [shape=circle label="Sn8\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nDIVERSE between frontEnd/version_2 and\nfrontEnd/version_3: cores 7/29, fault\ncontainment regions 4/11, core types\nppcE200/sparcLEON."];
  A3 [shape=ellipse style=filled fillcolor="#fff6d5" label="A3 (A)\nDistinct core types give distinct\ntoolchains and object code, not\nindependent design. Design independence\nremains an undischarged claim. The mapping\nevidence below establishes the deployment\nproperty only."];
  C13 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C13\nCandidate methods from the standard: IEC\n61508-7 A.7.6 information redundancy; IEC\n61508-7 A.13.2 cross-monitoring of\nmultiple actuators; IEC 61508-7 B.1.4\ndiverse hardware; IEC 61508-7 C.4.4\ndiverse programming"];
  G11 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G11\nAn IEC 61508 method realising Diverse\nRedundancy is implemented in frontEnd, and\nits effectiveness for the faults of\nconcern is demonstrated.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G12 [shape=box label="G12\nA disagreement among the versions is\ndetected before the result leaves the\ncomponent. [nvp_three_version/SC4]"];
  S6 [shape=parallelogram label="S6\nAchieved through the Comparison tactic\n(Checking): Detection of discrepancies of\nredundant system outputs."];
  C14 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C14\nComparison: Tests whether the outputs of\nfully redundant subsystems are equal in\norder to detect failures. Usually implies\nthe use of a redundancy tactic."];
  C15 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C15\nCandidate methods from the standard: IEC\n61508-7 A.1.3 comparator; IEC 61508-7\nA.6.5 input comparison/voting"];
  G13 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G13\nAn IEC 61508 method realising Comparison\nis implemented in frontEnd, and its\neffectiveness for the faults of concern is\ndemonstrated.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G14 [shape=box label="G14\nActor rasta of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 1, attains SIL 1 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C16 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C16\nrasta is unfolded into 1 concurrent copy,\nbound to core 13, implemented at SIL 1."];
  Sn9 [shape=circle label="Sn9\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of rasta is implemented\nat or above its allocated SIL and runs on\na core provisioned to at least that level."];
  G15 [shape=box label="G15\nEvery copy of rasta is implemented at SIL\n1 or above and is not hosted on a core\nprovisioned below that level."];
  S7 [shape=parallelogram label="S7\nArgument by development process alone: no\nstructural safety pattern is applied."];
  C17 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C17\nIEC 61508 expects diagnostic coverage from\nSIL 2 upward, so process alone is\nadmissible only to SIL 1 (Q20). The\nexploration enforced this ceiling when\nchoosing the pattern."];
  G16 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G16\nrasta is developed and verified to SIL 1\nin accordance with IEC 61508-3.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G17 [shape=box label="G17\nActor powspec of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 1, attains SIL 1 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C18 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C18\npowspec is unfolded into 1 concurrent\ncopy, bound to core 13, implemented at SIL\n1."];
  Sn10 [shape=circle label="Sn10\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of powspec is\nimplemented at or above its allocated SIL\nand runs on a core provisioned to at least\nthat level."];
  G18 [shape=box label="G18\nEvery copy of powspec is implemented at\nSIL 1 or above and is not hosted on a core\nprovisioned below that level."];
  S8 [shape=parallelogram label="S8\nArgument by development process alone: no\nstructural safety pattern is applied."];
  C19 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C19\nIEC 61508 expects diagnostic coverage from\nSIL 2 upward, so process alone is\nadmissible only to SIL 1 (Q20). The\nexploration enforced this ceiling when\nchoosing the pattern."];
  G19 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G19\npowspec is developed and verified to SIL 1\nin accordance with IEC 61508-3.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G20 [shape=box label="G20\nActor audspec of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 1, attains SIL 1 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C20 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C20\naudspec is unfolded into 1 concurrent\ncopy, bound to core 13, implemented at SIL\n1."];
  Sn11 [shape=circle label="Sn11\nIndependent re-check of the solution:\nevery active copy of audspec is\nimplemented at or above its allocated SIL\nand runs on a core provisioned to at least\nthat level."];
  G21 [shape=box label="G21\nEvery copy of audspec is implemented at\nSIL 1 or above and is not hosted on a core\nprovisioned below that level."];
  S9 [shape=parallelogram label="S9\nArgument by development process alone: no\nstructural safety pattern is applied."];
  C21 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C21\nIEC 61508 expects diagnostic coverage from\nSIL 2 upward, so process alone is\nadmissible only to SIL 1 (Q20). The\nexploration enforced this ceiling when\nchoosing the pattern."];
  G22 [shape=box style=dashed color="#b00020" label="G22\naudspec is developed and verified to SIL 1\nin accordance with IEC 61508-3.  <>UNDEVELOPED"];
  G23 [shape=box label="G23\nActor compJah of application c_rasta,\nallocated SIL 3, attains SIL 3 in the\ndeployed architecture."];
  C22 [shape=box style="rounded,filled" fillcolor="#f0f0f0" label="C22\ncompJah is unfolded into 1 concurrent\ncopy, bound to core 1, implemented at SIL\n3."];
